  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v5.8.16 - on SpawnDev.ILGPU 5.4.29. Wan 2.2: the VAE's spatial attention runs on the register-blocked GEMM: the decoder middle went from ~12.4 s to ~0.79 s per latent frame on an AMD RX 590 (OpenCL, 1280x704; measured by SpawnGen) and 1.0 s to 0.26 s on an RTX 4070 (CUDA), same results (env WAN_ATTN_GEMM=0 is the A/B). The pipeline's building blocks are public for callers running their own graph (e.g. a ComfyUI-style split graph): Wan22Pipeline.LoadWeightsAsync, LoadTokenizerAsync, TokenizePrompt and WanVae.GetLatentNormalizationAsync (the latent mean and std; checked against ComfyUI's own Wan 2.2 VAE: 1.9e-4). WanRequest.Trace now also times every VAE convolution. SpawnDev.ILGPU 5.4.29 fixes a CUDA miscompile of chained narrowing conversions such as (byte)(int)f. See CHANGELOG.md.",
